Deck: 
Cards 2-10 are "Infantry. They cost their number (Exm 10 is 10 points). They beat cards lower and lose to higher cards.
Aces are a instant kill of any card infront of it (On the first row) no matter the number and is dicared right after.
Face cards are Support. 
Support: You have a row behind your first row where support cards can be placed. They cost no points and have to abilities: 
+1 point for that round to spend on summons or discard to widen the board by one slot.
The support cards have no attack and no defence. They take a hit and are discarded.

Rules:
The front: Each team has three slots to place cards. This is then split into two rows. The first row is for numbered card/aces and is effected by aces.
The back row is for support cards only. the far back behind this line is the player's health which numbers 5 hit-points.

Draw: Each player draws cards back up to three.
Summon: Each player starts with ten points at the begining of each round. They can then spend those points on summoning numbered cards or can freely summon a support card.
When summoned, the cards are put into a slot face down.
Battle: Cards are flipped upright and the cards in each slot attack the opposing slot. The higher cards win the ingagement and stay on the slot. losing cards are discarded.
if a slot doesn't have a numbered card infront of it; then the attack is absorbed by the support in that slot. If there is not support card in the slot either; then the player loses one hit-point.
Reset: start a new round if no player has reached 0 hit-points.

Reasoning: We were confused the wholetime with the original and wanted a easy way to disurne cards. That led to the division of Aces/Numbered/Faces being their classes.
We made the steps easy and intuitive to anyone familiar with card games. leading to point system and slots. We wanted the game to not feel like a slot machine and a stalemate so we added the support system for flare.
The ace was made a "Bomb" so players could have some breaking of enemy plans. 

More will be changed in future iterations due to stalemates still acuring and a disire for more intreging gameplay.
